{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["In cattle it is written וקרבו וכרעיו, and in sheep it is written והקרב והכרעים. And it is taught in Tanna deBei Eliyahu: because when a small animal walks it raises its legs crosswise (like warp and woof), but a large animal raises its legs to its sides. And therefore a small animal's food changes in its stomach, and therefore its dung too differs from that of a large animal. In cattle it is written only והקטיר, and in sheep it is written והקריב והקטיר, because sheep are few and he brings and burns everything at once. In cattle הוא is not written, and in sheep and bird הוא is written, because the bird burnt offering comes in place of the cattle in poverty — one might think if he made it like cattle it would be valid, therefore הוא is written. In cattle לרצונו is written, and not in sheep and bird, because he increases to bring."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:47.287638001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}